4. Remote Exam Setup
The ECBA exam is an online remote proctored exam administered by IIBA’s exam
delivery partner, PSI.
You are expected to know the remote exam requirements and prepare ahead of time to
meet them.
Please review the following to understand the rules and procedures for taking the exam with online remote proctoring:
•
IIBA Guide to Online Proctored Exams for full technical and set-up requirements
•
PSI Online Proctoring Experience video showing the exam day experience
•
Exam Information for refunds, rescheduling, and accommodation requests
Personal Laptop/Computer
Do not use the company office or company laptop/computer to take your exam, as work environments and company computers often have firewalls and restrictions.
Government-Issued Photo Identification (ID)
The ID must be valid (not expired) and original (not a photocopy). Temporary ID is not accepted. It must be written in Western characters, showing your picture and signature.
Your first name and last name must match exactly in three places: your ID, IIBA profile name, and PSI name. There can be no differences. If your name does not match your identification, you must notify IIBA at certification@iiba.org . Only IIBA can make this update. All updates must be done at least one week before your scheduled exam, otherwise you won’t be able to take it.
The following identification is accepted:
•
Government-issued driver's licence
•
US Department of State driver's licence
•
National, state, or country-issued identification card
•
Government-issued passport
•
Passport card
Photo ID Capture for Check-in
For online remote proctored exams, you must take a picture of your photo ID at check-in or when scheduling the exam.
